Hi Chris and Eric,

Thanks for the replies.

Regarding prediction with covariates outside the range of values in the original model - yes that's a good point. To take care of that, in the map of predicted densities (attached here - probably should have included that with my original post), I place hatching over prediction cells where we have poor confidence in the prediction. Currently the hatching corresponds to areas where either 1) the CV is >= 2, or 2) where the prediction covariate is outside the range of values in the explanatory data. I currently also have hatching over the areas where CV = 0 as well, but am considering removing it if the variance of zero in those cells can be interpreted as "good prediction".

Dave

